    "uid": "2a75b78ee796195d669d2a60e372cfda",
    "title": "Service stopped or disabled",
    "desc": "A program stopped, disabled, masked or killed a systemd service, or triggered the magic SysRq key. Taking a service down is how an attacker disrupts availability or clears the way before acting (MITRE T1489): stopping cron to kill a defender's scheduled scan, stopping a database or app to force a restart into a tampered config, or SysRq-killing processes. The defense services have their own rules - disable_logging owns the logging stack, tamper_banken owns banken and auditd, disable_firewall the firewall, disable_mac AppArmor/SELinux - so this covers the rest, whatever is being stopped. A `systemctl restart` or `status` is not matched; a stop/disable/mask/kill is.",
